  YOUR instance's known-noisy entities.

  RULES + a short known-noise list only — no logs, no full run history.
  ========================================================================= -->

# Home Assistant health check — retained memory

## Connection
- Target: `${HASS_BASE_URL}` (your HA instance). Auth: `Bearer ${HASS_TOKEN}`.
- Read-only. GET requests only. Never call a service or change a state.

## Known-noisy entities (SUPPRESS — do not alert)
<!-- These are entities you have confirmed are *expected* to be flaky/absent.
     Listing one here means: do not report it as a finding. Replace with yours. -->
- `sensor.example_battery_powered_sensor` — sleeps to save battery; reports
  `unavailable` between wake cycles. Expected, not a fault.
- `binary_sensor.example_guest_phone` — only present when a guest device is on
  the network; `unknown` when away is normal.
- `weather.example_forecast_provider` — upstream API occasionally 5xx's;
  recovers on its own within an hour. Only alert if stuck > 6 h.

## Known-noisy log patterns (SUPPRESS)
- `WARNING ... example_integration ... retrying` — transient, self-heals.

## Behavioral rules
- Suppress anything matching the lists above. Report everything else.
- Never hide a *new* failure just to keep the report short.
- If a NEW entity has been `unavailable`/`unknown` across 3+ consecutive runs
  and the human has not acted, append it here as a candidate noisy entity and
  note the date — but keep reporting it until then.
- Prefer one terse all-clear line over a verbose "everything is fine" report.

